ROM Metadata Framework

This project contains original framework code licensed under the MIT License
unless otherwise noted.

The framework can integrate with independently installed third-party tools,
libraries, emulators, catalogues, and metadata services. Third-party projects
retain their own copyrights, trademarks, and licenses.

Current integration boundaries include:

- Dolphin Emulator command-line tooling for GameCube/Wii inspection and
  normalization;
- xdvdfs command-line tooling for original-Xbox XDVDFS inspection and
  normalization;
- rcheevos through a separately built helper executable;
- external catalogue and metadata-provider services.

The Python distribution does not bundle Dolphin, xdvdfs, the rcheevos helper,
commercial game content, or third-party metadata databases.

Repository-only integration material may include provenance records, helper
source, upstream license copies, and validation instructions. Those files do not
become part of the installed Python package unless explicitly included in a
future distribution.

Use of a project or product name does not imply ownership or endorsement.

Each material integration must document its upstream source, license,
integration method, supported version or revision where practical, and
redistribution status. See the repository licensing and third-party provenance
documentation for the authoritative project policy.
